  "body": "Found while fixing #600 (PR #607).\n\n**Today:** `trace/eye_geom.rs` `preview_camera` always casts perspective rays. In Orthographic mode the traced stock (the sim view) is drawn with perspective geometry, so it won't line up with the ortho-projected meshes, toolpaths and part.\n\n**Expected:** the traced stock casts parallel rays (origin across the view plane, a shared direction) when the viewport is orthographic, matching `Camera::mvp` / `ray_through`.\n\n**Done means:** a test that, in ortho, a known stock corner traced by the sim view lands on the same screen pixel as the mesh corner (within a pixel), and perspective is unchanged.",
